00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:58,810
Speaker 2: Or that you have recounted your position,.

227
00:15:58,970 --> 00:16:00,250
Speaker 1: You have denied the faith.

228
00:16:08,410 --> 00:16:10,530
Speaker 1: That a Christian will stand in front.

229
00:16:10,530 --> 00:16:13,450
Speaker 2: Of his parents, start hurling insults.

230
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:21,930
Speaker 1: Many interesting things we see today.

231
00:16:23,610 --> 00:16:29,930
Speaker 2: A man will stand in front of his wife, punch her in the eyes, on the nose,.

232
00:16:36,490 --> 00:16:37,050
Speaker 1: Listen.

233
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,940
Speaker 1: And Paul was saying this to a church.

234
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:42,220
Speaker 1: It means there are some people in church who do foolish things like this.

235
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:47,660
Speaker 1: And let me they can now sit in the false comfort.

236
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:49,100
Speaker 1: I know who I am.

237
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:50,620
Speaker 1: I'm the righteousness of God in Christ.

238
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:51,820
Speaker 1: You are an imposter.

239
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:53,020
Speaker 2: That's what he's saying.

240
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:56,580
Speaker 2: He said, you are worse than an infidel.

241
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:57,900
Speaker 1: You don't do stuff like that.

242
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:08,569
Speaker 2: And so we must not come to a point where our knowledge of grace stops us from holding people accountable.

